gr=dict(t='Grammar – Prepositions and Adverbs; Personification', p=[
 'Preposition: shows the relation of a noun/pronoun with other words (direction, place, time) – at school, between two friends, about numbers.',
 'A preposition is always followed by an object (noun/pronoun): She ran up the stairs.',
 'An adverb tells more about the verb and has no object: She rang me up. / He stepped inside.',
 'The same word (on, off, up, down, in, outside, along) can be a preposition or an adverb – check whether a noun follows it.',
 'Personification: giving human qualities to a non-living thing. The River speaks, laughs and advises, so it is written with a capital “R” like a person’s name.',
 'Sound words: shrieked, splashed, murmuring, sob, rustle, gasped, rattling, noisy, wailed.',
 'Borrowed words: catamaran (Tamil “kattu maram” = tied wood), guru and karma (Sanskrit), chutney and jungle (Hindi).']),
